{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChJp3RGv7pQAQ2AzJeMao","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`ccode(sinc(x))` now prints the Piecewise form suggested in the issue:\n\n```\n((Ne(x, 0)) ? (\n   sin(x)/x\n)\n: (\n   1\n))\n```\n\nThe cause was that the C printer had no handler for `sinc`, so it fell through to the \"Not supported in C\" fallback. I added a `_print_sinc` method to `sympy/printing/ccode.py` that rewrites `sinc(arg)` as `Piecewise((sin(arg)/arg, Ne(arg, 0)), (1, True))` and prints that.\n\nThe existing tests in `sympy/printing/tests/test_ccode.py` pass (30 passed). I didn't add a test for `sinc`, since the rules say not to touch test files."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":920,"cache_read_input_tokens":19386,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":920},"output_tokens":251,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4d0c8679-f45e-4def-a785-334d3dff2ac3","uuid":"9cf324fe-5ad7-4119-bc4f-e0d20ada9b12","timestamp":"2026-11-22T23:11:21.784Z","request_id":"req_011ChJp3R8yu2ynKEqTK6toS"}
